\section{Exclusions and errors}{

Per-group declaration outcomes are returned rather than thrown. Stable reason
codes are \code{included}, \code{scope_dataset}, \code{scope_file_group},
\code{reserved_provenance_column}, \code{term_missing}, \code{variable_missing},
\code{no_declared_files}, \code{unsupported_format}, \code{invalid_timezone}, and
\code{incomplete_datetime}; each has a plain-language message.

Invalid argument types, empty values, duplicates, and inconsistent
\code{variable_scope}/selector combinations error before planning. Programmatically
useful condition subclasses include \code{glcdp_unknown_dataset},
\code{glcdp_unknown_file_group}, \code{glcdp_unknown_term}, \code{glcdp_unknown_variable},
\code{glcdp_collection_plan_revision}, \code{glcdp_collection_plan_provenance},
\code{glcdp_collection_plan_ambiguous_variable},
\code{glcdp_collection_plan_relationship}, \code{glcdp_collection_plan_serialization},
and \code{glcdp_collection_plan_id}. Term labels that are not canonical ids are
reported as unknown terms rather than matched ambiguously.
